      "type": "about",
      "tabLabel": "About",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Backbone",
          "subtitle": "Patience",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Backbone is a difficult two-pack patience game built around a central backbone reserve, with the objective of moving all cards onto foundations."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Backbone is known as a unique and difficult solitaire because its long reserve structure creates deep sequencing problems."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "One player lays out the central reserve, tableau, stock, and foundations."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Use two shuffled standard packs."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two standard 52-card decks, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal the backbone reserve and supporting tableau, then use the remaining cards as stock."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
